263
00:14:27,620 --> 00:14:29,220
Where did you hear a word like that, Runa?

264
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:32,400
It's always been the four of us playing together.

265
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:34,980
Why should we bother letting that girl in now?

266
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:41,220
I swear I'm going to kick her out of our guild if it's the last thing I do.

267
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,400
Hmm...

268
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:49,100
Hey!

269
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:51,480
We're headed the same way, so let's go home together!

270
00:14:52,180 --> 00:14:57,140
I impulsively blurted that out, but the conversation's not taking off like I'd hoped.

271
00:14:58,440 --> 00:14:59,400
Hey, Yamada?

272
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:00,440
Yes?

273
00:15:01,140 --> 00:15:04,040
So tell me, do you all often hang out together like this?

274
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:04,660
Yes.

275
00:15:04,900 --> 00:15:05,180
Huh.

276
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:07,240
So you must really get along.

277
00:15:07,580 --> 00:15:08,300
I guess so.

278
00:15:08,300 --> 00:15:11,160
Oh, hey, Eta sure is a fun guy, huh?

279
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:12,600
He is.

280
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:16,300
Okay, then...

281
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:34,840
You're not hurt, are you?

282
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:35,680
Sorry.

283
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:38,200
You should switch places with me.

284
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:39,300
It's okay.

285
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:40,280
I feel bad.

286
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:41,040
It's fine.

287
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:42,960
Thank you very much.

288
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:45,840
Uh...

289
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:46,140
Huh?

290
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:47,840
Oh.

291
00:15:48,860 --> 00:15:49,380
Ah.

292
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:50,620
It's him.

293
00:15:51,740 --> 00:15:52,140
Whoa.

294
00:15:52,620 --> 00:15:55,000
For a second there, I thought they were staring at me.

295
00:15:57,060 --> 00:15:59,980
I was taken aback by his good looks at first, too.

296
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:04,280
Could it be that you're really in love with Yamada?

297
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:05,760
Oh.

298
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:09,560
When she looked at us, is that what she saw?

299
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:11,040
Not good, not good.

300
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:13,180
Yamada's a valued online gamer friend.

301
00:16:13,940 --> 00:16:16,040
Say, uh, Yamada, what are you having for dinner?

302
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:18,280
Well, I'm not really all that hungry.

303
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:19,020
Really?

304
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:20,500
Pudding, maybe.

305
00:16:21,800 --> 00:16:22,640
That's funny.

306
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:26,920
That will be 128 yen.

307
00:16:28,020 --> 00:16:29,620
Thanks for shopping with us.

308
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:30,900
Uh, wait.

309
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:32,900
So you were being serious about that?

310
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:33,520
Yes.

311
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:36,840
Do you live alone, Yamada?

312
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:38,060
Yes.

313
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:39,420
And you don't cook at home?

314
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:40,540
Not at all.

315
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:41,720
What?

316
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:43,180
I almost can't believe it.

317
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:44,180
What do you eat every day?

318
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:47,300
I buy food from convenience stores and stuff.

319
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:48,820
Oh, really?

320
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:52,640
Yamada's a high school student, if I'm remembering right.

321
00:16:54,100 --> 00:16:56,320
Doesn't his mom say anything about that?

322
00:16:57,760 --> 00:16:58,280
No.

323
00:16:58,280 --> 00:17:00,860
I shouldn't pry into someone's family life.

324
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:03,120
Hmm.

325
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:05,060
Uh, Yamada!

326
00:17:05,460 --> 00:17:06,520
Do you have some time?

327
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:07,720
